eir commands and configurations to use the new flag name.\n./CHANGELOG.md:2480:  The option is related to `--resume` for `claude` command and has an entirely different meaning from `--auto-continue` mode. This rename makes the distinction clearer and aligns the terminology with the resume functionality.\n./CHANGELOG.md:2483:  - Replace `--auto-continue-on-limit-reset` with `--auto-resume-on-limit-reset` in all commands\n./CHANGELOG.md:2600:- 5030fe1: Fix --auto-continue-on-limit-reset flag not working\n./CHANGELOG.md:2602:  When Claude hit its usage limit with --auto-continue-on-limit-reset enabled, the code would exit early\n./CHANGELOG.md:2605:  This patch adds a condition to skip the failure exit when limit is reached with auto-continue enabled,\n./CHANGELOG.md:2612:- 6d7fb43: Add --auto-continue-on-limit-reset option to hive command\n./CHANGELOG.md:2614:  The hive command was missing the --auto-continue-on-limit-reset option that is available\n./CHANGELOG.md:2700:  - Remove obsolete options (--fork, --auto-fork, --auto-continue) from /help command\n./CHANGELOG.md:2704:  - Fix README.md defaults for --auto-fork and --auto-continue (now true)\n./CHANGELOG.md:3325:- dca5bed: Make --auto-continue enabled by default\n./CHANGELOG.md:3326:  - Changed default value from false to true for --auto-continue in both hive and solve commands\n./CHANGELOG.md:3328:    - When -s is used, auto-continue is automatically disabled to avoid conflicts\n./CHANGELOG.md:3329:    - Explicit --auto-continue with -s shows proper error message\n./CHANGELOG.md:3330:    - Users can still use --no-auto-continue to explicitly disable\n./tests/test-telegram-bot-dry-run.mjs:108:  --auto-continue\n./tests/test-telegram-bot-dry-run.mjs:121:      args: ['--token', 'test_token_123', '--solve-overrides', '(--auto-continue --attach-logs)', '--dry-run'],\n./tests/test-telegram-bot-dry-run.mjs:156:      args: ['--token', 'test_token_123', '--no-hive', '--solve-overrides', '(--auto-continue --verbose)', '--