ue-1177/raw-data/issue-1143.json:3:  \"body\": \"Add experimental `/merge` command, that accepts repository link, and checks all issues with `ready` label (if no such label configured for the repository, and we have permissions to configure it should configure such label with description). `Is ready to be merged`. As labels are shared with pull requests also it should work with pull requests the same way.\\n\\nSo if label is on issue - we do get pull request linked to the issue, like we do with `/solve --auto-continue` and add it to merge queue.\\nIf the label on pull request - we just go and add pull request to the merge queue.\\n\\nWhat it does it actually pretty simple, it sorts all `ready` pull requests by creation time, and first merges one, that was created first (minimum of pull request and its linked issue creation date), it monitors for CI/CD, once it is finished and is successful it continues to merge pull requests on by one.\\n\\nWe work only with `ready`, but not yet merged pull requests their issues. `ready` but closed - should be ignored.\\n\\nMaking sure no pull requests are merged at the same time, and each one is merged after previous CI/CD successfully finished (meaning all CI/CDs the repository, to guarantee no interference will be with each merge/release).\\n\\nSo it should be simple but helpful feature. That should work only if there are all nessesary permissions.\",\n./experiments/test-claude-md-check.mjs:4:// This script tests the new auto-continue feature that checks for missing CLAUDE.md\n./experiments/test-claude-md-check.mjs:12:    'issue-54-branch1': false, // CLAUDE.md missing - should auto-continue immediately\n./experiments/test-claude-md-check.mjs:14:    'issue-54-branch3': false, // CLAUDE.md missing - should auto-continue immediately\n./experiments/test-claude-md-check.mjs:46:// Test the new auto-continue logic\n./experiments/test-claude-md-check.mjs:72:          console.log(`   🎯 Selected this PR for auto-continue`);\n./experiments