udy with timeline, root cause analysis, and downloaded log data\\n\\n### Before\\n```\\n📊 Limit Information\\n- Reset Time: 4:00 PM\\n```\\n\\n### After\\n```\\n📊 Limit Information\\n- Reset Time: in 14m (Feb 6, 3:00 PM UTC)\\n```\\n\\n## Files Changed\\n\\n| File | Changes |\\n|------|---------|\\n| `src/config.lib.mjs` | Increase default buffer to 10 min, add `jitterMs` config |\\n| `src/solve.auto-continue.lib.mjs` | Add random jitter to wait time calculation |\\n| `src/github.lib.mjs` | Use `formatResetTimeWithRelative()` for reset time in PR comments |\\n| `src/solve.mjs` | Use `formatResetTimeWithRelative()` for reset time in waiting comment |\\n| `tests/test-limit-reset-config.mjs` | Tests for buffer, jitter, and formatting |\\n| `docs/case-studies/issue-1236/` | Case study with timeline and raw data |\\n\\n## Test plan\\n\\n- [x] New test suite `tests/test-limit-reset-config.mjs` (12 tests passing)\\n- [x] Existing `tests/test-usage-limit.mjs` (63 tests passing)\\n- [x] Existing `tests/limits-display.test.mjs` (18 tests passing)\\n- [x] Prettier formatting checks pass\\n- [x] One pre-existing test failure in `solve-queue.test.mjs` (unrelated THRESHOLD naming test)\\n\\nFixes #1236\\n\\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\",\n./docs/case-studies/issue-1446/README.md:18:3. No actual reset time information is provided to the user\n./docs/case-studies/issue-1446/README.md:59:- Uses same `dayjs` formatting as other reset times for consistency\n./docs/case-studies/issue-1573/consensus-stuck-excerpt.txt:6:[2026-04-11T00:24:27.042Z] [STDOUT] api.github.com/users/konard/repos\",\"events_url\":\"https://api.github.com/users/konard/events{/privacy}\",\"received_events_url\":\"https://api.github.com/users/konard/received_events\",\"type\":\"User\",\"user_view_type\":\"public\",\"site_admin\":false},\"created_at\":\"2026-03-29T15:01:14Z\",\"updated_at\":\"2026-03-29T15:01:14Z\",\"body\":\"## 🤖 Solution Draft Log\\nThis log file contains the com