\"Usage Limit\\\\\\\" docs/case-studies -S || true\\nsed -n '1,160p' docs/case-studies/issue-719-usage-limit/INDEX.md | tee logs.case-study.index.head.txt || true\\nsed -n '1,160p' docs/case-studies/issue-719-usage-limit/20-TIMELINE.md | tee logs.case-study.timeline.head.txt || true\\\"\",\"aggregated_output\":\"total 52\\ndrwxrwxr-x  2 hive hive 4096 Nov 13 04:48 .\\ndrwxrwxr-x 15 hive hive 4096 Nov 13 04:04 ..\\n-rw-rw-r--  1 hive hive 5425 Nov 13 04:20 00-OVERVIEW.md\\n-rw-rw-r--  1 hive hive 4809 Nov 13 04:01 01-ERROR-PATTERNS.md\\n-rw-rw-r--  1 hive hive 7218 Nov 13 04:01 02-IMPLEMENTATION-PLAN.md\\n-rw-rw-r--  1 hive hive 4270 Nov 13 04:20 03-EVIDENCE.md\\n-rw-rw-r--  1 hive hive 2233 Nov 13 04:48 10-LOGS.md\\n-rw-rw-r--  1 hive hive 1606 Nov 13 04:48 20-TIMELINE.md\\n-rw-rw-r--  1 hive hive  443 Nov 13 04:48 INDEX.md\\ndocs/case-studies/issue-719-usage-limit/00-OVERVIEW.md:1:# Case Study: Usage Limit Error Handling (Issue #719)\\ndocs/case-studies/issue-719-usage-limit/00-OVERVIEW.md:88:### 2. Usage Limit Result Flag\\ndocs/case-studies/issue-719-usage-limit/00-OVERVIEW.md:104:## ⏳ Usage Limit Reached\\ndocs/case-studies/issue-719-usage-limit/00-OVERVIEW.md:134:⏳ Usage Limit Reached!\\ndocs/case-studies/issue-719-usage-limit/INDEX.md:1:# Case Study Index: Usage Limit Handling (Issue #719)\\ndocs/case-studies/issue-719-usage-limit/01-ERROR-PATTERNS.md:5:### Pattern 1: Usage Limit Error (from issue #719)\\ndocs/case-studies/issue-719-usage-limit/01-ERROR-PATTERNS.md:108:    await log('\\\\n\\\\n⏳ Usage Limit Reached!', { level: 'warning' });\\ndocs/case-studies/issue-719-usage-limit/01-ERROR-PATTERNS.md:134:### Test Case 1: Usage Limit with Reset Time\\ndocs/case-studies/issue-719-usage-limit/02-IMPLEMENTATION-PLAN.md:86:## ⏳ Usage Limit Reached\\ndocs/case-studies/issue-719-usage-limit/02-IMPLEMENTATION-PLAN.md:120:⏳ Usage Limit Reached!\\ndocs/case-studies/issue-719-usage-limit/02-IMPLEMENTATION-PLAN.md:133:### Step 1: Create Usage Limit Detection Module\\ndocs/case-studies/issue-719-usage-limit/03-EVIDENCE.md:38:## Usage Limit Evidence (From Issue Logs)\\ndocs/case-studies/issue-719-usage-limit/03-EVIDENCE.md:51:- `attachLogToGitHub()` in `src/github.lib.mjs` formats a dedicated \\\"Usage Limit Reached\\\" PR/issue comment including reset time, session ID, resume instructions, and log details when `--attach-logs` is used.\\ndocs/case-studies/issue-719/case-study.md:1:# Case Study: Usage Limit Handling Across Tools (Issue #719)\\ndocs/case-studies/issue-719/case-study.md:24:- In `src/solve.mjs`, when a tool run fails, pass `isUsageLimit`, `limitResetTime`, `toolName`, and a `resumeCommand` to `attachLogToGitHub`. This triggers a dedicated \\\"Usage Limit Reached\\\" comment with reset-time and clear resume instructions. Generic `errorMessage` is sent only when not a usage-limit case.\\n# Case Study Index: Usage Limit Handling (Issue #719)\\n\\n- 00-OVERVIEW.md — Executive summary, problem, solution, and testing plan\\n- 10-LOGS.md — Key log excerpts and references captured during investigation\\n- 20-TIMELINE.md — Chronological sequence of events with timestamps and SHAs\\n\\nRelated resources:\\n- Issue: https://github.com/deep-assistant/hive-mind/issues/719\\n- Pull Request: https://github.com/deep-assistant/hive-mind/pull/722\\n\\n# Timeline\\n\\n- 2025-11-12T11:47:04Z — Usage-limit error observed in external logs (see ci-logs/issue-719.json:1):\\n  - Message: \\\"You've hit your usage limit… try again at 12:16 PM.\\\"\\n  - Impact: Command appeared as success while actually failing due to usage limits.\\n\\n- 2025-11-13T03:54:27Z — Local run reproduction and enhanced tracing (see ci-logs/pr-722.details.txt:1):\\n  - Output: \\\"Weekly limit reached ∙ resets 5am\\\"\\n  - Exit: Reported failure path detected (CLI previously exited with code 0, now surfaced via PR comment formatting and failure branch).\\n  - Session: Captured a session ID for resumption.\\n\\n- 2025-11-13T04:17Z–04:34Z — CI validation on branch issue-719-a653aae7d4d5 (see ci-logs/gh-run-list.branch.json:1):\\n  - Multiple runs succeeded, confirming the new usage-limit handling and PR comment behavior are stable.\\n  - Latest successful head SHA: 419e64bc6c6ac88b8660d2cd44dba0dd2a833f4e\\n\\n# Root Causes\\n\\n- Usage-limit errors were not treated as a first-class failure mode across all tools.\\n- Reset time and resume instructions were not consistently surfaced to the user.\\n- PR comment formatter lacked a dedicated usage-limit variant; some flows showed generic success/failed formatting.\\n\\n# Fix Summary\\n\\n- Added detect-and-format path for usage limits in claude, codex, and opencode libs.\\n- Propagated limitResetTime and resumeCommand into attachLogToGitHub with a dedicated usage-limit comment.\\n- Made gist fallback prefer usage-limit formatting whenever isUsageLimit=true.\\n- solve.mjs now assigns global.limitResetTime from tool results for auto-continue-limit and PR comments.\\n\\n\",\"exit_code\":0,\"status\":\"completed\"}}\n./docs/case-studies/issue-729-codex-loop/rapid-loop-pattern.txt:8:8021:[2025-11-13T05:30:17.477Z] [INFO] {\"type\":\"item.completed\",\"item\":{\"id\":\"item_24\",\"type\":\"command_execution\",\"command\":\"bash -lc \\\"sed -n '1,200p' docs/case-studies/issue-719/case-study.md | tee logs.case-study.legacy.head.txt\\\"\",\"aggregated_output\":\"# Case Study: Usage Limit Handling Across Tools (Issue #719)\\n\\n## Summary\\n- Problem: When usage limits are reached for AI tools (Claude, Codex, OpenCode), the run was surfaced as a success comment with exit code 0, confusing users. PR comments also lacked a clear “limit reached” message and reset-time guidance.\\n- Impact: Users had to dig into logs to discover rate/usage limits. Comment formatting did not distinguish usage-limit from generic failures.\\n- Resolution: Detect usage-limit results and post a dedicated PR comment with reset time and resume instructions; mark the run as failure for CI clarity; attach logs when `--attach-logs` is used.\\n\\n## Timeline\\n- 2025-11-12 11:47:04Z: Session starts. Error: \\\"You've hit your usage limit... try again at 12:16 PM.\\\" (see issue body)\\n- 2025-11-13 03:54:27Z: Claude returns a result with `subtype: success` but `is_error: true` and text \\\"Weekly limit reached ∙ resets 5am\\\" (see related comment logs). The harness detected an error, but exit code remained 0 and comment formatting looked like success.\\n- 2025-11-13 03:58:40Z: Maintainer notes missing proper handling for weekly limit and missing reset-time in PR comment.\\n\\n## Data\\n- Issue JSON: issue-719.json\\n- Linked comment (ideav-local-associative-js): link-foundation-ideav-local-associative-js-pr2-comment-3521528245.json (+ .txt)\\n- Linked comment (hh-questions): konard-hh-questions-pr30-comment-3525165717.json (+ .txt)\\n\\n## Root Cause\\n- The tool libraries (Claude, Codex, OpenCode) already detect usage limits and expose `limitReached` and `limitResetTime`.\\n- The main driver (`solve.mjs`) attached PR logs on failure but always used the generic failure template, never activating the dedicated usage-limit template available in `attachLogToGitHub`.\\n- In some sessions, the underlying CLI reported `is_error: true` with exit code 0. The harness treated it as error internally, but the PR comment still resembled a success log.\\n\\n## Fix Implemented\\n- In `src/solve.mjs`, when a tool run fails, pass `isUsageLimit`, `limitResetTime`, `toolName`, and a `resumeCommand` to `attachLogToGitHub`. This triggers a dedicated \\\"Usage Limit Reached\\\" comment with reset-time and clear resume instructions. Generic `errorMessage` is sent only when not a usage-limit case.\\n- Exit remains non-zero on failure, ensuring CI and status reflect failure rather than success.\\n\\n## Proposed Additional Improvements\\n- Ensure the error-handlers also pass usage-limit context if an exception is thrown after a limit condition was previously detected.\\n- Expand `extractResetTime` patterns if new vendor messages emerge.\\n- Consider adding unit tests for formatting functions in `usage-limit.lib.mjs` and comment template activation in `github.lib.mjs`.\\n\\n## How to Resume\\n- The PR comment now includes a ready-to-run resume command when a session ID is available, e.g.:\\n  - `node src/solve.mjs <issue-url> --resume <session-id>`\\n\\n\",\"exit_code\":0,\"status\":\"completed\"}}\n./docs/case-studies/issue-729-codex-loop/rapid-loop-pattern.txt:12:8029:[2025-11-13T05:30:25.680Z] [INFO] {\"type\":\"item.started\",\"item\":{\"id\":\"item_27\",\"type\":\"command_execution\",\"command\":\"bash -lc \\\"ls -la src | sed -n '1,200p'\\nrg -n \\\\\\\"attachLogToGitHub|Usage Limit Reached|isUsageLimit|limitResetTime|extractResetTime\\\\\\\" src -S | tee logs.search-src-usage.txt\\\"\",\"aggregated_output\":\"\",\"exit_code\":null,\"status\":\"in_progress\"}}\n./docs/case-studies/issue-729-codex-loop/rapid-loop-pattern.txt:13:8031:[2025-11-13T05:30:25.757Z] [INFO] {\"type\":\"item.completed\",\"item\":{\"id\":\"item_27\",\"type\":\"command_execution\",\"command\":\"bash -lc \\\"ls -la src | sed -n '1,200p'\\nrg -n \\\\\\\"attachLogToGitHub|Usage Limit Reached|isUsageLimit|limitResetTime|extractResetTime\\\\\\\" src -S | tee logs.search-src-usage.txt\\\"\",\"aggregated_output\":\"total 880\\ndrwxrwxr-x  3 hive hive  4096 Nov 13 04:01 .\\ndrwxrwxr-x 14 hive hive 12288 Nov 13 05:30 ..\\n-rw-rw-r--  1 hive hive  2695 Nov 13 04:01 buildUserMention.lib.mjs\\n-rw-rw-r--  1 hive hive 60576 Nov 13 04:01 claude.lib.mjs\\n-rw-rw-r--  1 hive hive 11768 Nov 13 04:01 claude.prompts.lib.mjs\\n-rw-rw-r--  1 hive hive 20115 Nov 13 04:01 codex.lib.mjs\\n-rw-rw-r--  1 hive hive 11023 Nov 13 04:01 codex.prompts.lib.mjs\\n-rw-rw-r--  1 hive hive  7685 Nov 13 04:01 config.lib.mjs\\n-rw-rw-r--  1 hive hive  8078 Nov 13 04:01 contributing-guidelines.lib.mjs\\n-rw-rw-r--  1 hive hive  5510 Nov 13 04:01 exit-handler.lib.mjs\\n-rw-rw-r--  1 hive hive  4359 Nov 13 04:01 git.lib.mjs\\n-rw-rw-r-