rrors, 11 warnings (unchanged existing warnings).\\\\n- Verified experiments/usage-limit-demo.mjs and parse-reset-time.mjs.\\\\nIf anything else is needed (e.g., trimming warnings or adding a small parser test), I can follow up quickly.\\\\n\\\",\\\"createdAt\\\":\\\"2025-11-13T05:02:11Z\\\",\\\"id\\\":\\\"IC_kwDOPUU0qc7SITOo\\\"}\\nci-logs/pr-722.comments.latest.json:18:{\\\"author\\\":{\\\"login\\\":\\\"konard\\\"},\\\"body\\\":\\\"Follow-up for #719: Added robust detection for Claude’s weekly limit phrasing (e.g., ‘Weekly limit reached ∙ resets 5am’) and normalized reset-time extraction across tools. Also extended parseResetTime to accept ‘5am’ without minutes.\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\nThis ensures PR comments show the correct reset time and that --auto-continue-limit can wait until the proper time. CI is running for the latest commit; I’ll monitor and address any issues if they appear.\\\",\\\"createdAt\\\":\\\"2025-11-13T05:16:52Z\\\",\\\"id\\\":\\\"IC_kwDOPUU0qc7SIgU3\\\"}\\nci-logs/pr-722.comments.latest.json:19:{\\\"author\\\":{\\\"login\\\":\\\"konard\\\"},\\\"body\\\":\\\"CI for the latest commit is running; monitoring until completion. Summary of the final changes for #719:\\\\n\\\\n- Robust Claude weekly-limit detection (e.g., “Weekly limit reached ∙ resets 5am”) and normalized reset-time extraction across tools.\\\\n- Parse reset times like “5am” without minutes; normalize to HH:MM AM/PM for auto-continue.\\\\n- PR comments for usage limits now include reset time, session ID, and resume instructions; gist fallback always uses the usage-limit template.\\\\n- Case study docs and experiments updated and referenced in the PR body.\\\\n\\\\nIf any job fails, I will download the logs to ci-logs/ and propose a targeted fix.\\\\n\\\",\\\"createdAt\\\":\\\"2025-11-13T05:20:05Z\\\",\\\"id\\\":\\\"IC_kwDOPUU0qc7SIjFm\\\"}\\nci-logs/pr-722.comments.latest.json:20:{\\\"author\\\":{\\\"login\\\":\\\"konard\\\"},\\\"body\\\":\\\"CI is green for the latest head (8d356a2). Summ