[2026-04-15T18:58:10.424Z] [INFO] e --state merged --search [keywords].\\ndocs/case-studies/pr-4-revert-issue/session2_log.txt:412:          \\\"command\\\": \\\"gh issue view https://github.com/link-foundation/test-anywhere/issues/3 --json title,body,comments --jq '{title, body, comments: [.comments[] | {author: .author.login, createdAt: .createdAt, body: .body}]}'\\\",\\ndocs/case-studies/pr-4-revert-issue/session2_log.txt:448:          \\\"command\\\": \\\"gh pr view 4 --repo link-foundation/test-anywhere --json title,body,comments,state,isDraft --jq '{title, body, state, isDraft, comments: [.comments[] | {author: .author.login, createdAt: .createdAt, body: .body}]}'\\\",\\ndocs/case-studies/pr-4-revert-issue/session2_log.txt:484:          \\\"command\\\": \\\"gh pr checks 4 --repo link-foundation/test-anywhere\\\",\\ndocs/case-studies/pr-4-revert-issue/session2_log.txt:549:        \\\"content\\\": \\\"Test on Bun\\\\tpass\\\\t5s\\\\thttps://github.com/link-foundation/test-anywhere/actions/runs/18517975879/job/52772092615\\\\t\\\\nTest on Deno\\\\tpass\\\\t9s\\\\thttps://github.com/link-foundation/test-anywhere/actions/runs/18517975879/job/52772092620\\\\t\\\\nTest on Node.js\\\\tpass\\\\t6s\\\\thttps://github.com/link-foundation/test-anywhere/actions/runs/18517975879/job/52772092651\\\",\\ndocs/case-studies/pr-4-revert-issue/session2_log.txt:1484:        \\\"content\\\": \\\"[issue-3-8560e169 1611137] Merge CI and CD into single workflow with version check\\\\n 3 files changed, 89 insertions(+), 116 deletions(-)\\\\n create mode 100644 .github/workflows/ci-cd.yml\\\\n delete mode 100644 .github/workflows/publish.yml\\\\n delete mode 100644 .github/workflows/test.yml\\\\nTo https://github.com/link-foundation/test-anywhere.git\\\\n   2637748..1611137  issue-3-8560e169 -> issue-3-8560e169\\\",\\ndocs/case-studies/pr-4-revert-issue/session2_log.txt:1629:          \\\"command\\\": \\\"gh pr edit 4 --repo link-foundation/test-anywhere --body \\\\\\\"$(cat <<'EOF'\\\\n## Summary\\\\n\\\\nThis PR adds a unified CI/CD workflow that automatically publishes the `test-anywhere` package to NPM, but only after all tests pass successfully and only if the current version is not already published on NPM.\\\\n\\\\n## Changes\\\\n\\\\n- **New unified workflow file**: `.github/workflows/ci-cd.yml`\\\\n  - Runs on all pushes to `main` branch and on all pull requests\\\\n  - Tests across Node.js, Bun, and Deno runtimes in parallel\\\\n  - Only publishes to NPM on `main` branch pushes after all test jobs complete successfully\\\\n  - Checks if the current package version already exists on NPM before publishing\\\\n  - Uses `NPM_TOKEN` secret for authentication\\\\n  \\\\n- **Removed separate workflows**: Deleted `test.yml` and `publish.yml` in favor of single unified workflow\\\\n\\\\n- **Version bump**: Updated `package.json` from `0.1.0` to `0.1.1` to prepare for next release\\\\n\\\\n## How it works\\\\n\\\\n1. On every push to `main` or PR, all three test jobs (Node.js, Bun, Deno) run in parallel\\\\n2. On `main` branch pushes, if all tests pass, the publish job runs (due to `needs: [test-node, test-bun, test-deno]`)\\\\n3. The publish job checks if the current version in `package.json` is already published on NPM\\\\n4. Only if the version is not published yet, the package is published to NPM with public access\\\\n5. If the version already exists, publishing is skipped with a message\\\\n\\\\n## Prerequisites\\\\n\\\\nBefore this workflow can successfully publish, a repository administrator needs to:\\\\n1. Generate an NPM access token with publish permissions\\\\n2. Add it as a repository secret named `NPM_TOKEN` in Settings → Secrets and variables → Actions\\\\n\\\\n## Testing\\\\n\\\\n- All existing tests pass locally and in CI\\\\n- Workflow YAML syntax is valid\\\\n- Publishing step will be tested on first merge to main with a new version number\\\\n\\\\nFixes #3\\\\n\\\\n---\\\\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\\\\nEOF\\\\n)\\\\\\\"\\\",\\ndocs/case-studies/pr-4-revert-issue/session2_log.txt:1660:        \\\"content\\\": \\\"https://github.com/link-foundation/test-anywhere/pull/4\\\",\\ndocs/case-studies/pr-4-revert-issue/session2_log.txt:1805:          \\\"command\\\": \\\"sleep 10 && gh pr checks 4 --repo link-foundation/test-anywhere\\\",\\ndocs/case-studies/pr-4-revert-issue/session2_log.txt:1836:        \\\"content\\\": \\\"Publish to NPM\\\\tskipping\\\\t0\\\\thttps://github.com/link-foundation/test-anywhere/actions/runs/18532609532/job/52819173985\\\\t\\\\nTest on Bun\\\\tpass\\\\t7s\\\\thttps://github.com/link-foundation/test-anywhere/actions/runs/18532609532/job/52819157076\\\\t\\\\nTest on Deno\\\\tpass\\\\t7s\\\\thttps://github.com/link-foundation/test-anywhere/actions/runs/18532609532/job/52819157124\\\\t\\\\nTest on Node.js\\\\tpass\\\\t6s\\\\thttps://github.com/link-foundation/test-anywhere/actions/runs/18532609532/job/52819157085\\\",\\ndocs/case-studies/pr-4-revert-issue/session2_log.txt:1920:        \\\"content\\\": \\\"Already up to date.\\\\nFrom https://github.com/link-foundation/test-anywhere\\\\n * branch            main       -> FETCH_HEAD\\\",\\ndocs/case-studies/pr-4-revert-issue/session2_log.txt:2009:          \\\"command\\\": \\\"gh pr diff 4 --repo link-foundation/test-anywhere > /tmp/pr-diff.txt 2>&1 && head -200 /tmp/pr-diff.txt\\\",\\ndocs/case-studies/pr-4-revert-issue/session2_log.txt:2110:          \\\"command\\\": \\\"gh pr list --repo link-foundation/test-anywhere --state merged --limit 2 --json number,title,body\\\",\\ndocs/case-studies/pr-4-revert-issue/session2_log.txt:2286:          \\\"command\\\": \\\"gh pr ready 4 --repo link-foundation/test-anywhere\\\",\\ndocs/case-studies/pr-4-revert-issue/session2_log.txt:2317:        \\\"content\\\": \\\"✓ Pull request link-foundation/test-anywhere#4 is marked as \\\\\\\"ready for review\\\\\\\"\\\",\\ndocs/case-studies/pr-4-revert-issue/session2_log.txt:2462:          \\\"command\\\": \\\"gh pr comment 4 --repo link-foundation/test-anywhere --body \\\\\\\"$(cat <<'EOF'\\\\n## Implementation Complete\\\\n\\\\nI've successfully merged the CI and CD workflows into a single unified workflow as requested.\\\\n\\\\n### Changes Made\\\\n\\\\n1. **Created `.github/workflows/ci-cd.yml`** - A unified CI/CD workflow that:\\\\n   - Runs tests on all three platforms (Node.js, Bun, Deno) for every push to main and every PR\\\\n   - Only attempts to publish on pushes to the main branch\\\\n   - Checks if the current version already exists on NPM before publishing\\\\n   - Only publishes if all tests pass AND the version is not yet published\\\\n\\\\n2. **Removed old workflows**:\\\\n   - Deleted `.github/workflows/test.yml`\\\\n   - Deleted `.github/workflows/publish.yml`\\\\n\\\\n### How It Works\\\\n\\\\n- On PRs: All tests run in parallel (as you can see in the checks above)\\\\n- On pushes to main: All tests run, and if they all pass, the publish job checks NPM\\\\n  - If the current package version (0.1.1) is not published → publishes to NPM\\\\n  - If the version already exists → skips publishing with a message\\\\n\\\\n### CI Status\\\\n\\\\n✅ All tests passing:\\\\n- Test on Node.js: ✅ Pass (6s)\\\\n- Test on Bun: ✅ Pass (7s)\\\\n- Test on Deno: ✅ Pass (7s)\\\\n- Publish to NPM: ⏭️ Skipping (as expected on PR)\\\\n\\\\nThe PR is now ready for review and merge.\\\\n\\\\n---\\\\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\\\\nEOF\\\\n)\\\\\\\"\\\",\\ndocs/case-studies/pr-4-revert-issue/session2_log.txt:2493:        \\\"content\\\": \\\"https://github.com/link-foundation/test-anywhere/pull/4#issuecomment-3406796950\\\",\\ndocs/case-studies/pr-4-revert-issue/session2_log.txt:2546:          \\\"command\\\": \\\"gh pr view 4 --repo link-foundation/test-anywhere --json url,title,state,isDraft,mergeable --jq '{url, title, state, isDraft, mergeable}'\\\",\\ndocs/case-studies/pr-4-revert-issue/session2_log.txt:2577:        \\\"content\\\": \\\"{\\\\\\\"isDraft\\\\\\\":false,\\\\\\\"mergeable\\\\\\\":\\\\\\\"MERGEABLE\\\\\\\",\\\\\\\"state\\\\\\\":\\\\\\\"OPEN\\\\\\\",\\\\\\\"title\\\\\\\":\\\\\\\"Add CD workflow to publish to NPM when all tests pass\\\\\\\",\\\\\\\"url\\\\\\\":\\\\\\\"https://github.com/link-foundation/test-anywhere/pull/4\\\\\\\"}\\\",\\ndocs/case-studies/pr-4-revert-issue/session2_log.txt:2596:        \\\"text\\\": \\\"Perfect! Let me create a summary of the completed work:\\\\n\\\\n## Summary\\\\n\\\\nI've successfully completed the implementation based on the user's feedback. Here's what was accomplished:\\\\n\\\\n### Key Changes\\\\n\\\\n1. **Unified CI/CD Workflow** - Created `.github/workflows/ci-cd.yml` that:\\\\n   - Runs tests on all three platforms (Node.js, Bun, Deno) in parallel\\\\n   - Executes on both PRs and pushes to main\\\\n   - Only runs the publish job on main branch pushes after all tests pass\\\\n   - Checks if the current version exists on NPM before attempting to publish\\\\n   - Skips publishing if the version already exists\\\\n\\\\n2. **Removed Separate Workflows** - Deleted the old `test.yml` and `publish.yml` files\\\\n\\\\n3. **Version Check Logic** - Added a step that queries NPM to verify whether the current package version is already published, ensuring we don't attempt to re-publish existing versions\\\\n\\\\n### Current Status\\\\n\\\\n✅ **All tasks completed**:\\\\n- All CI checks passing (Node.js, Bun, Deno tests all pass)\\\\n- PR is mergeable\\\\n- PR marked as ready for review\\\\n- Changes follow the repository's commit and PR style\\\\n\\\\n**Pull Request**: https://github.com/link-foundation/test-anywhere/pull/4\\\\n\\\\nThe implementation now meets all requirements from issue #3:\\\\n- Single CI/CD workflow (not separate CI and CD)\\\\n- Publishes only if the current version is not already published on NPM\\\\n- Publishes only if all tests pass\\\"\\ndocs/case-studies/pr-4-revert-issue/session2_log.txt:2624:  \\\"result\\\": \\\"Perfect! Let me create a summary of the completed work:\\\\n\\\\n## Summary\\\\n\\\\nI've successfully completed the implementation based on the user's feedback. Here's what was accomplished:\\\\n\\\\n### Key Changes\\\\n\\\\n1. **Unified CI/CD Workflow** - Created `.github/workflows/ci-cd.yml` that:\\\\n   - Runs tests on all three platforms (Node.js, Bun, Deno) in parallel\\\\n   - Executes on both PRs and pushes to main\\\\n   - Only runs the publish job on main branch pushes after all tests pass\\\\n   - Checks if the current version exists on NPM before attempting to publish\\\\n   - Skips publishing if the version already exists\\\\n\\\\n2. **Removed Separate Workflows** - Deleted the old `test.yml` and `publish.yml` files\\\\n\\\\n3. **Version Check Logic** - Added a step that queries NPM to verify whether the current package version is already published, ensuring we don't attempt to re-publish existing versions\\\\n\\\\n### Current Status\\\\n\\\\n✅ **All tasks completed**:\\\\n- All CI checks passing (Node.js, Bun, Deno tests all pass)\\\\n- PR is mergeable\\\\n- PR marked as ready for review\\\\n- Changes follow the repository's commit and PR style\\\\n\\\\n**Pull Request**: https://github.com/link-foundation/test-anywhere/pull/4\\\\n\\\\nThe implementation now meets all requirements from issue #3:\\\\n- Single CI/CD workflow (not separate CI and CD)\\\\n- Publishes only if the current version is not already published on NPM\\\\n- Publishes only if all tests pass\\\",\\ndocs/case-studies/pr-4-revert-issue/pr4_details.json:1:{\\\"body\\\":\\\"## Summary\\\\n\\\\nThis PR adds a unified CI/CD workflow that automatically publishes the `test-anywhere` package to NPM, but only after all tests pass successfully and only if the current version is not already published on NPM.\\\\n\\\\n## Changes\\\\n\\\\n- **New unified workflow file**: `.github/workflows/ci-cd.yml`\\\\n  - Runs on all pushes to `main` branch and on all pull requests\\\\n  - Tests across Node.js, Bun, and Deno runtimes in parallel\\\\n  - Only publishes to NPM on `main` branch pushes after all test jobs complete successfully\\\\n  - Checks if the current package version already exists on NPM before publishing\\\\n  - Uses `NPM_TOKEN` secret for authentication\\\\n  \\\\n- **Removed separate workflows**: Deleted `test.yml` and `publish.yml` in favor of single unified workflow\\\\n\\\\n- **Version bump**: Updated `package.json` from `0.1.0` to `0.1.1` to prepare for next release\\\\n\\\\n## How it works\\\\n\\\\n1. On every push to `main` or PR, all three test jobs (Node.js, Bun, Deno) run in parallel\\\\n2. On `main` branch pushes, if all tests pass, the publish job runs (due to `needs: [test-node, test-bun, test-deno]`)\\\\n3. The publish job checks if the current version in `package.json` is already published on NPM\\\\n4. Only if the version is not published yet, the package is published to NPM with public access\\\\n5. If the version already exists, publishing is skipped with a message\\\\n\\\\n## Prerequisites\\\\n\\\\nBefore this workflow can successfully publish, a repository administrator needs to:\\\\n1. Generate an NPM access token with publish permissions\\\\n2. Add it as a repository secret named `NPM_TOKEN` in Settings → Secrets and variables → Actions\\\\n\\\\n## Testing\\\\n\\\\n- All existing tests pass locally and in CI\\\\n- Workflow YAML syntax is valid\\\\n- Publishing step will be tested on first merge to main with a new version number\\\\n\\\\nFixes #3\\\\n\\\\n---\\\\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\\\",\\\"comments\\\":[{\\\"author\\\":{\\\"login\\\":\\\"konard\\\"},\\\"authorAssociation\\\":\\\"MEMBER\\\",\\\"body\\\":\\\"## 🤖 Solution Draft Log\\\\n\\\\nThis log file contains the complete execution trace of the AI solution draft process.\\\\n\\\\n📎 **Log file uploaded as GitHub Gist** (138KB)\\\\n🔗 [View complete solution draft log](https://gist.github.com/konard/b1d5083bdb3297d8013ced7ee0a3104f)\\\\n\\\\n---\\\\n*