rt watch mode if enabled OR if we need to handle uncommitted changes\\n   867\\t  if (argv.verbose) {\\n   868\\t    await log('');\\n   869\\t    await log('🔍 Auto-restart debug:', { verbose: true });\\n   870\\t    await log(`   argv.watch (user flag): ${argv.watch}`, { verbose: true });\\n   871\\t    await log(`   shouldRestart (auto-detected): ${shouldRestart}`, { verbose: true });\\n   872\\t    await log(`   temporaryWatch (will be enabled): ${shouldRestart && !argv.watch}`, { verbose: true });\\n   873\\t    await log(`   prNumber: ${prNumber || 'null'}`, { verbose: true });\\n   874\\t    await log(`   prBranch: ${prBranch || 'null'}`, { verbose: true });\\n   875\\t    await log(`   branchName: ${branchName}`, { verbose: true });\\n   876\\t    await log(`   isContinueMode: ${isContinueMode}`, { verbose: true });\\n   877\\t  }\\n   878\\t\\n   879\\t  // If uncommitted changes detected and auto-commit is disabled, enter temporary watch mode\\n   880\\t  const temporaryWatchMode = shouldRestart && !argv.watch;\\n\",\"exit_code\":0,\"status\":\"completed\"}}\n./docs/case-studies/issue-729-codex-loop/solve-2025-11-13T04-00-57-948Z.log.part-01:4294:[2025-11-13T05:34:42.346Z] [INFO] {\"type\":\"item.completed\",\"item\":{\"id\":\"item_47\",\"type\":\"agent_message\",\"text\":\"Summary of progress\\n- On branch: issue-719-a653aae7d4d5 (up to date with origin)\\n- Reviewed PR 722 comments and latest updates\\n- CI status: latest 5 runs are passing for head SHA caa19eb\\n- Lint: 0 errors, 12 warnings (preexisting)\\n- No further code changes required; PR is already marked ready (isDraft: false)\\n\\nWhat I verified\\n- Usage-limit handling is implemented across all tools:\\n  - Claude: src/claude.lib.mjs:1116 detects limit via detectUsageLimit; formats user-facing message; returns flags and reset time.\\n  - Codex: src/codex.lib.mjs:398+ detects usage limit; formats message; returns limit flags and reset time.\\n  - OpenCode: src/opencode.lib.mjs:334+ detects usage limit; formats message; returns limit flags and reset time.\\n- GitHub comment formatter supports separate usage-limit template with resume instructions and gist fallback:\\n  - src/github.lib.mjs: usage-limit branch builds the dedicated comment, includes reset time, session ID, and gist fallback for long logs.\\n- solve.mjs integrates the isUsageLimit flow and passes flags to the comment attachment:\\n  - src/solve.mjs:825 passes isUsageLimit, limitResetTime, toolName, resumeCommand to attachLogToGitHub.\\n- Case study docs for issue #719 are present and linked:\\n  - docs/case-studies/issue-719-usage-limit/INDEX.md, 00-OVERVIEW.md, 01-ERROR-PATTERNS.md, 10-LOGS.md, 20-TIMELINE.md.\\n\\nCI investigation protocol (checked)\\n- Listed recent runs for the branch and matched head SHA: ci-logs/gh-run-list.branch-latest.json, ci-logs/pr-722.head-sha.txt\\n- All runs after the head commit are “success”; no failures to download logs for.\\n\\nLocal repo state\\n- There are tracked snapshot/log files updated locally (ci-logs.* and logs.*) as part of verification; these aren’t required for code functionality. I did not commit them to avoid churn in the PR since CI is green and the PR body has already been synced by the last push.\\n\\nNext steps\\n- If you want, I can:\\n  - Commit refreshed ci-logs snapshots to mirror current CI metadata.\\n  - Tackle the lint warnings (cosmetic) across a few files.\\n  - Add a tiny parser smoke-check to CI for usage-limit detection.\\n\\nOtherwise, this is ready for review/merge as implemented.\"}}\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
