[2026-04-15T18:59:36.466Z] [INFO] 2026-04-15T18:59:36.465777Z DEBUG session_loop{thread_id=019d9281-c409-7723-9d23-b132497f2f69}:submission_dispatch{otel.name="op.dispatch.user_input" submission.id="019d9281-c429-7422-a653-25db0966869e" codex.op="user_input"}:turn{otel.name="session_task.turn" thread.id=019d9281-c409-7723-9d23-b132497f2f69 turn.id=019d9281-c429-7422-a653-25db0966869e model=gpt-5.4}: codex_core::stream_events_utils: Output item item=Message { id: Some("msg_02a7aabe1a68410e0169dfe0145da481918009d5beeeabab83"), role: "assistant", content: [OutputText { text: "Implemented the fix on `issue-1614-2fe968881d10` and pushed it to PR 1615: https://github.com/link-assistant/hive-mind/pull/1615\n\nThe root cause was in [`src/solve.validation.lib.mjs`](/tmp/gh-issue-solver-1776279295749/src/solve.validation.lib.mjs): the auto-resume parser only accepted time-only strings, so `Apr 17, 4:00 AM` threw `Invalid time format`. I updated it to strip an optional month/day prefix before parsing, and added a regression test in [`tests/test-solve-validation-reset-time.mjs`](/tmp/gh-issue-solver-1776279295749/tests/test-solve-validation-reset-time.mjs) covering both `parseResetTime` and `calculateWaitTime`.\n\nVerified locally with `node tests/test-solve-validation-reset-time.mjs` and `npm run test:usage-limit`. Working tree is clean, and the PR title/description now reflect the actual fix, reproduction, and verification." }], end_turn: None, phase: Some(FinalAnswer) }
